course: dictionary
lesson: 4237
title: Grandma: a word and a name
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Grandma is a noun, a word that names a person, place or thing. It means the mother of your mother or of your father. In «Priya's grandma in Leicester smiles», the words around it show that grandma is a person who smiles.
explain: The same word can also be a name you call someone. In «Hi, Grandma!», the greeting and the exclamation mark show you are talking to her directly, so Grandma is used as a name and starts with a capital letter.
explain: Other words mean the same as grandma, such as granny, gran, nana, nan and grandmother. Try swapping one into a sentence. «Grandma knits you a jumper» still makes sense with nana, so they are synonyms here.
fact: Grandma is a noun: a grandma, grandmas.
fact: Grandma means the mother of your mother or of your father.
fact: When Grandma is used as a name, write it with a capital G, as in «Grandma, this is Tom.»
fact: Other words for grandma include granny, gran, nana, nan and grandmother.
fact: Phrases you may meet include Grandma's house, visit Grandma and great-grandma.
exercise: In «Priya's grandma in Leicester smiles», what is grandma? | A feeling | *A person | A city | A kind of food
exercise: Which word is another word for grandma? | *Nana | Pyjamas | Bungalow | Shampoo
exercise: In «Hi, Grandma!», why does Grandma start with a capital letter? | *Because it is used as a name | Because it is a verb | Because it is a place | Because every noun starts with a capital letter
test: In «Tucker's grandma in Pittsburgh takes him to church every Sunday», what kind of word is grandma? | A place name | *A noun for a person | An adjective | A verb
test: Which word is NOT another word for grandma? | Granny | Nan | Gran | *Grandpa
exam: Which sentence uses Grandma as a name? | *«Hi, Grandma!» | «Grandma's house is blue.» | «My grandma lives in Leicester.» | «A grandma is a noun.»
